WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.334
-Will Farrell, everybody!
Come on!

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.133
Thank you for being here!
-Thank you!

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:07.634
-Thank you for
coming back to the show

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:08.701
and enjoy yourself, guys.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.434
Yeah, thanks.
The -- The -- Will.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.701
-Jimmy, aren't you just lost
in the holiday magic?

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.434
-Yes, I am.
Was this --

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.467
Was this what you're
bringing us here?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:18.767
What is this you brought?

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:23.200
-Well, Jimmy, you know I have
a passion for miniatures

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.400
because I'm a bit of
a control freak.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.534
-Okay. Yeah.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:30.734
-So every January
I begin construction

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:33.901
of my perfect Christmas village.
-Oh.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.734
-And since the holidays
are almost here,

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.267
I thought it would be
fun to bring it here

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.801
and share it with all of you.
-Oh, my God. This is --

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.868
Thank you, this --
-Yeah.

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.701
-It's really impressive.
What --

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.934
-I haven't even shown you
the best part yet.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.968
Look.
[ Switch clicks ]

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.467
-Wow! Look at that!
-Ohh.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.634
-Wow, that's very good.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.234
-Would you like for me
to give you a tour?

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.334
-I would love to
see a tour of this.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:00:59.501
-Oh, oh, okay.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.701
If you do the honor
of sprinkling a little

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.300
Christmas snow...

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.434
-Uh-huh.
-Okay.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.467
...over the village.
-Over the village, sure.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.834
-And fellas, can I get some
music that says

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.300
"Holiday magic?"

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.234
Oh, thank you. Okay.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.234
Welcome to my perfect
Christmas village.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.501
-Wow.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:22.100
-The season starts downtown
with our village gazebo.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.501
-Oh!

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:26.334
And look here,
a friendly snowball fight.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.534
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.100
Incredible detail.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.567
Who's this guy over here?

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.834
-Oh! That's Michael
the Popcorn Man.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.000
-Oh.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.734
And who is she?

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.767
-Oh, that's Francine.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.767
She's the town heartbreaker.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.601
But it's not just the people
that make a Christmas village

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:45.634
perfect...
-Uh-huh.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.567
-...look at these
darling shops here.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:48.667
-Uh-huh. Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.567
I see you have
a post office there.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.934
-Yeah.
-You have a hardware store.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:55.200
-And don't forget to buy
all your Christmas cigars

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.067
at the cigar shop.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.367
Mmm.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:00.667
Is there anything that says
holiday cheer

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.400
like the smell of
a Christmas cigar?

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.133
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.767
-I guess, I guess.
Sure, I guess.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.400
I never, uh...
-You guess?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.400
I know.
-Oh, okay, you do?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.400
-Yeah.
You know?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.701
Crap, I've never heard of that.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.801
What is this factory over here?
This is a factory?

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.133
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah?

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:18.033
They make toys there?
Or candy canes or something?

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.167
-No. Nobody knows
what goes on there.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.467
Not even me.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.868
-What's this over here?

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.968
-Oh! That's the
Ross Dress For Less.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.868
And, uh, and that's
where the towns people

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.868
shop when they want dresses.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:36.767
-But for less.
-But for less.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:38.234
-Yeah, I gotcha.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:42.434
-Uh, over here we have people
getting their photos with Santa.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:46.067
But you better be good,
or no Christmas cigars for you.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.067
And here's our
reindeer petting zoo.

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:52.067
-Oh, that's got --
Oh, it looks like there's some

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.200
are there some wolves
in there with the reindeer?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.300
-Uh-huh.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.300
Well, Santa's busy
with other things,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.501
so the wolves are there
to keep the reindeer in check.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.667
-Uh, it looks like some wolves
have actually escaped

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:03.901
and are walking around town.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:08.501
-Well, they vote, so they've
earned their right to be there.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.000
-The wolves --
The wolves vote?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.334
-The wolves run the town, Jimmy.
They run it all.

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.934
So you better not say
anything bad about them.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.467
[ Panting, heaving ]

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.234
Hey, [ Whimpering ]

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.133
it's not almost midnight, is it?

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.901
[ Panting ]

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.467
-It -- It --

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.534
It i-- It i--

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.534
It i-- It is.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.033
-Oh, no.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.133
-[ Laughing ]
-Oh. Oh, no!

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.901
Not on the full moon!

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.367
Not now!

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.400
Ahh!

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.734
It burns!

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.434
-Oh, oh, oh.
What -- What -- Will!

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:47.534
What's going on?

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.634
-I'm turning into a werewolf.

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:52.300
[ Grunting, gurgling ]

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.934
And I told a fib.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:59.400
That's not the original
Michael the Popcorn Man.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.567
I ate the real Michael.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:02.901
-What?

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:07.901
-I woke up the next morning
in the gazebo... naked.

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:12.701
I couldn't remember anything,
but I could taste popcorn man.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:15.200
You have to take me
to the factory!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.734
Take me to the factory and
handcuff me to the radiator

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.334
for your own safety!

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.067
[ Grunting, gurgling continues ]

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.100
-Wait, wait, wait!
Is that all I can --

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.167
-[ Grumbling, growling ]
-Is that

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.400
Is that all I can do?

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.567
-It's a long process.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.400
-This is terrible.
What can I do?!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.234
-The village needs blood!
Needs new, fresh blood!

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:36.300
-What?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.467
-Oh, I have an idea!
I have an idea!

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.501
I have a tiny figurine of me.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.200
-Oh.
-Maybe if I put him in

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.000
your Christmas village,
that could be good?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.567
-It's the only way!
[ Breathing heavily ]

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.667
-Look at there.
-Jimmy --

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.667
[ Applause ]

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.567
Jimmy, I told another fib.
-What?

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:58.334
-I wasn't really
turning into a werewolf.

00:04:58.334 --> 00:04:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:03.467
-I just needed to see
if you had Christmas heart.

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.667
And I needed to know if you
could save my village,

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.033
and you did it!

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:09.033
You saved Christmas!

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:10.801
Holiday cigar?

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:13.734
-Wow! Thanks, buddy!
-Yeah?

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:16.100
Will Farrell, everybody.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.167
More with Will after the break.
Come on back!

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.734
Oh, my God!

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.534
Oh, my -- What?

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

